<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roger II of Sicily</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1095">1095</a>–1154</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roger II was Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from 1105, then united the Norman lands of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> by taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, Capua, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. He was crowned the first king of Sicily in 1130. His court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> mixed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, Greek and Arab culture and employed the geographer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-idrisi">al-Idrisi</a>, and his fleets seized the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> as a Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily.jpg" alt="Roger II of Sicily" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthias Süßen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martorana_Palermo_msu2017-0166.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
